  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HOM&apos;s FUND 2025-Community Media Network</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Media Network is an independent media NGO seeking to serve the Jordanian community through an enlightening discourse. Their mission is to encourage dialogue, educate the public, help in the decision-making process, and empower the marginalized groups by managing media and cultural projects throughout the Kingdom of Jordan. This project aims to celebrate the 25th anniversary of their website AmmanNet, by hosting a conference on community radio in the Arab world. The conference will focus on critical issues facing community media today - such as how to secure funding, navigate governmental restrictions, and leveraging social media. This conference will also look at the future role of community-based, not-for-profit media in empowering marginalized communities and safeguarding the freedom of expression.</narrative>
  </description>
